// Title: Execution via WorkFolders.exe
// Sigma ID: 0bbc6369-43e3-453d-9944-cae58821c173
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Maxime Thiebaut (@0xThiebaut)
// Date: 2021-10-21 | Modified: 2022-12-25
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1218
// Description: Detects using WorkFolders.exe to execute an arbitrary control.exe
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate usage of the uncommon Windows Work Folders feature.
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/elliotkillick/status/1449812843772227588
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_susp_workfolders.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\control.exe" and InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\WorkFolders.exe") and (not(FolderPath =~ "C:\\Windows\\System32\\control.exe"))
